From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:57:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(delegation): a Claude route runs on its parent chat's
 API-key provider

A delegation.backends.<backend>.options entry marked family: claude is a Claude route. When the parent chat runs on an Anthropic API-key provider (api_mode anthropic_messages on api.anthropic.com, not claude-pool), the route keeps its model and runs on that provider instead of its own, so the account the user picked pays for the chat's subagents. Any other chat, and every route not marked claude, resolves as before. A subagent carries its chat's choice to its own subagents and a restart handoff records it. A route that fails never falls back to the other side.
